{
  "id": "grammar.a2.imperativoafirmativo.03.formal",
  "title": "Formal Commands (usted / ustedes)",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "When speaking politely to someone you address as 'usted' (or a group 'ustedes'), the command forms switch their vowel: -AR verbs take -e / -en, and -ER/-IR verbs take -a / -an (from the present subjunctive)."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Formal Command Endings",
      "rows": [
        [
          "hablar (-ar)",
          "hable (ud.) / hablen (uds.)"
        ],
        [
          "comer (-er)",
          "coma (ud.) / coman (uds.)"
        ],
        [
          "escribir (-ir)",
          "escriba (ud.) / escriban (uds.)"
        ],
        [
          "pasar (-ar)",
          "pase (ud.) / pasen (uds.)"
        ],
        [
          "tomar (-ar)",
          "tome (ud.) / tomen (uds.)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Señor García, pase adelante, por favor.",
          "english": "Mr. García, come forward, please."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Tomen asiento, señores.",
          "english": "Take a seat, gentlemen."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Firme aquí con bolígrafo.",
          "english": "Sign here with pen."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Common irregulars in formal commands match the yo-form stem: tener → tenga, venir → venga, poner → ponga, decir → diga, hacer → haga."
    }
  ]
}